    board: file CF-387 (step-2 footprint cost) and CF-388 (gateway_auth dies on a fresh node) — dogfood walk 2026-11-08
    
    Walked README Quick start at pinned origin/main 40db7d8 in a git-archive copy of
    that SHA, because two sibling lanes held the shared checkout. Steps 1 and 3 reach
    repo-convention rows and CF-145's fix holds; the two rows filed here are what the
    walk found that no row owned.
    
    CF-387 — layer 00 of README step 2 spends 29.85 s of a 48.48 s run inside
    node_hygiene.py's footprint row (31.97 s standalone), walking $HOME/.hermes
    (131 GB) against a 5 GiB admission floor, while project-node.sh:242-246 claims
    the row "stays cheap on a host with a large $HOME".
    
    CF-388 — on a live node created by the documented path, layer 20's gateway_auth
    staging dies with FileNotFoundError on ~/.hermes/config.yaml.cf-tmp: the config
    file's parent directory is never created (:79-83, while :64 creates only the
    password file's directory). gateway_start then refuses the public bind, so the
    behaviour README.md:50-51 promises is unreachable on a fresh node. Re-running the
    writer after the adapter creates ~/.hermes passes, so the defect is the
    precondition and its ordering, not the writer.
    
    The node was reaped in the same tick (destroy rc=0, local key removed, id absent
    from the post-destroy census).
    
    Addresses CF-387, CF-388. Evidence: docs/audits/code-factory-dogfood-2026-11-08-04-02-17.md
    
